You have.  The key is:
> 1332.       if (obj->blessed && !rnl(4))

rnl is the luck-adjusted random number generator from rnd.c

If I'm doing my math right, with luck of 12 you'll have a 2.6% chance
of failing this test, so .25 *.026 = about a .6% chance of any blessed
+2 projectile disappearing when used.  Curiously, luck higher than 12
is worse than luck=12 for this purpose because of the "if (Luck &&
rn2(50 - Luck)) {" test.  But I could be slightly off.

The main point is that rnl skews things very heavily based on luck.

rnl:
int
rnl(x)      /* 0 <= rnl(x) < x; sometimes subtracting Luck */
register int x; /* good luck approaches 0, bad luck approaches (x-1)
*/
{
    register int i;

#ifdef DEBUG
    if (x <= 0) {
        impossible("rnl(%d) attempted", x);
        return(0);
    }
#endif
    i = RND(x);

    if (Luck && rn2(50 - Luck)) {
        i -= (x <= 15 && Luck >= -5 ? Luck/3 : Luck);
        if (i < 0) i = 0;
        else if (i >= x) i = x-1;
    }

    return i;
}


